Subject: [PATCH] cli: candidate polls share one recent read of the candidate tables

A candidate query polls the controller's candidate tables (get_sta, the whole
station tree, about 70 ms with 50 clients) under the native lock every 10 to
100 ms until its reply arrives. With queries to four agents at once the
polls kept the lock busy: in the fifty-client room a round took 6.6 s at the
median, queries queued 0.6 s for the lock and some timed out (HTTP 504).

A poll takes a read no older than 100 ms, and polls arriving together wait
for one read (candidate_coordination.go). The query's baseline stays its own
read, so a shared read can only delay seeing a reply, never make an older
measurement look new.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
+++ b/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
@@ -4699,7 +4699,9 @@
     var observedErrors []candidateLinkError
     for attempt := 0; time.Now().Before(deadline); attempt++ {
         if r.Context().Err() != nil { return }
-        all, allErrors, completions, err := readState()
+        // polls share one recent read of the candidate tables (candidate_coordination.go)
+        state := sharedCandidateState.read(timing, candidateStateShareAge, time.Now)
+        all, allErrors, completions, err := state.metrics, state.rejected, state.completions, state.err
         if err == nil {
             observed = observed[:0]
